  "feedback_interpretation": "The previous outcomes shift this round toward testing response curves around demonstrated failures. Diethyl malonate was much earlier than predicted at both 10/1 and 50/1, whereas methoxyethyl acetoacetate, the acetoacetate-bearing methacrylate, and the separated aromatic diketone were substantially later, especially in V2. This strongly supports topology-specific learning and motivates a limited reproducibility check for malonate. Sulfoxide measurements resolved the former reversed-onset prediction: retention increased markedly from 1/1 to 5/1, with the main historical failure at 5/1. Basic nitrogen compounds were generally underpredicted, but nicotinate and nitroacetophenone did not support a common upward correction. Matched dimethoxytoluene and methylenedioxyacetophenone measurements contradicted their predicted intermediate-solvent maxima. Ortho-methoxyacetophenone showed that loading confounded part of the earlier interpretation, and its low-load 20/1 versus 50/1 observations still discourage imposing universal monotonicity. Nitrobenzophenone supplied a particularly informative loading contrast: onset moved earlier while completion moved later. Finally, methyl salicylate finished at 9.05 mL in pure EA rather than the predicted 20.66 mL, while salicylaldehyde's 26.73 mL completion was close to prediction; the shared strong-eluent hypothesis therefore needs narrowing. These are acquisition-time errors, not current residuals. Current predictions have changed after retraining, so follow-up choices test whether those corrections generalize.",
